# step 9.3: kube-prometheus-stack findings, all permanent/non-actionable via values -
# each is how the chart's constituent tools are fundamentally designed to work, not a
# misconfiguration. unlike step 8.4's backend/frontend LOW findings (handled via a plain
# severity filter, since those really can never change), these are CRITICAL/HIGH and worth
# tracking explicitly as accepted risk, matching the infra repo's step 8.3 .trivyignore
# convention (id + reason + review date) rather than silently widening the severity filter.

# prometheus-operator's own RBAC: it watches/manages Prometheus, Alertmanager, ServiceMonitor,
# etc. cluster-wide by design - narrowing this breaks service discovery across namespaces.
